{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033788-newbie-mage-st-looking-for-sleeper-to-awakened-tips","id":1033788,"title":"Newbie Mage ST Looking For Sleeper to Awakened Tips","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T18:42:47-08:00","id":1033788,"title":"Newbie Mage ST Looking For Sleeper to Awakened Tips","content":"Hello!<br /> So I'm writing on a wip Mage 2E campaign about a small group of highschoolers who'll starts as Sleepers and becoming Awakened at the end of first gaming session. I look for the feel of a YA book turning more into a eldritch terror some kind of story, bc I generally like the idea of having the players as teens who doesn't think of the consequences of their discovered powers.<br /> <br /> Here's the big problem: I have a total creativeblock figuring out what will be the cause of their Awakening. Preferably something they will have in common so I can bring them together as a playergroup, like a supernatural entity or a weird phenomena at school that will cause enough chock to triggering their Awakening. I'm not sure if they're legit reasons, I'm still trying to get through the damn prestigious corebook *waves fists*.<br /> <br /> If those ideas sucks then I'd love to hear some better advice or possible ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Learn to know my own garbage PCs at <a href=\"http://damnedcitylights.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">damnedcitylights.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12883-cosmic_leeches","name":"cosmic_leeches","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T18:48:15-08:00","id":1033794,"title":"","content":"Ask your players how they want their Awakenings to look like and figure out the common theme by talking with them about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T02:32:08-08:00","id":1033930,"title":"","content":"Or look through <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/78098/Night-Horrors-The-Unbidden\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Night Horrors: Unbidden</b></a> book - it has cool 'monsters' for <b>Mage</b> games, centered on the theme of magic being alive AND dangerous. I used Gnomon for fresh mage players, but it's more proper mage danger. There should be other cool 'problems' there, that could easily trigger Awakening of multiple characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T05:03:50-08:00","id":1033961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033788-newbie-mage-st-looking-for-sleeper-to-awakened-tips?p=1033794#post1033794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask your players how they want their Awakenings to look like and figure out the common theme by talking with them about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe as simple as that, sometimes I get too carried away writing the fluff that I forget my players opinions and such <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033788-newbie-mage-st-looking-for-sleeper-to-awakened-tips?p=1033930#post1033930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or look through <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/78098/Night-Horrors-The-Unbidden\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Night Horrors: Unbidden</b></a> book - it has cool 'monsters' for <b>Mage</b> games, centered on the theme of magic being alive AND dangerous. I used Gnomon for fresh mage players, but it's more proper mage danger. There should be other cool 'problems' there, that could easily trigger Awakening of multiple characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent! I'll look after that book as soon as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Learn to know my own garbage PCs at <a href=\"http://damnedcitylights.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">damnedcitylights.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12883-cosmic_leeches","name":"cosmic_leeches","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:23:31-08:00","id":1034022,"title":"","content":"It skews a bit younger than high schoolers for the most part, but the WoD book Innocents has plenty of story concepts which can be easily adapted for older kids. Beyond that, check out practically any episode from the first few seasons of Buffy the Vampire Slayer, or movies like Chronicle and The Faculty for idea mining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}